# Build symlinks created by `nix build` / `nixos-rebuild build`. These point
# into /nix/store and change on every build, so tracking them means the tree
# is permanently dirty and every nix command prints "Git tree is dirty".
result
result-*

# Scratch clones / checkouts of other projects that sometimes get made inside
# this repo. Not part of the config; ignored so they stop showing up as
# untracked noise in `git status`.
/ng-check/

# Debris that lands in the repo root from working on the agent stack. Ignored
# rather than tidied by hand because both kinds reappear, and neither is
# something you want swept up by a `git add -A`:
#
#   cookie jars written by `curl -c` while poking hermes-webui - these hold a
#   live `hermes_session` token, i.e. an actual credential
#   Hermes session exports (`hermes sessions export`), NDJSON with one object
#   per message and named <date>_<time>_<hash> - conversation transcripts,
#   which are neither configuration nor anything to publish
/cj*.txt
/[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]_[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]_*
